{{!
    @template assignsubmission_refchecker/export_pdf_header

    The cover block of the downloadable report: what it is about, and the aggregate counts.

    This template is rendered into TCPDF's writeHTML(), NOT into a browser. TCPDF understands only
    a small fixed subset of HTML and loads no stylesheet, so classes do nothing here: use inline
    style attributes, and only color, background-color, font-size, font-weight, text-align, border
    and width. There is no flexbox, grid or float, so any columns must be a table with an explicit
    percentage width on every cell, because TCPDF's automatic widths are unreliable.

    One exception to "style everything with CSS": cellpadding is read by TCPDF only as an
    attribute (tcpdf.php getHtmlDomArray), so it stays an attribute here even though HTML5 calls it
    obsolete and the Mustache linter says so.

    All values other than the admin authored strings come from external databases, so this template
    uses HTML escaping variables throughout and never triple-brace ones.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * heading string - the report heading
    * assignmentlabel string - the label for the assignment name
    * assignment string - the assignment name
    * subjectlabel string - "Student" or "Group"
    * subject string - who the report is about
    * checkedlabel string - the label for when checking finished
    * checked string - when checking finished, empty when it has not
    * downloadedlabel string - the label for when this file was made
    * downloaded string - when this file was made
    * iscomplete bool - whether checking finished
    * statuslabel string - the localised status line
    * hassectionheading bool - whether the reference list heading is known
    * sectionheading string - which section of the document was read
    * istruncated bool - whether the reference list was truncated
    * truncatednotice string - the truncation notice
    * stats array - the aggregate counts, as label and value pairs
    * hasretracted bool - whether any reference is retracted
    * retractedlabel string - the label for the retracted count
    * retracted int - how many references are retracted
    * haspredatory bool - whether any reference is possibly predatory
    * predatorylabel string - the label for the predatory count
    * predatory int - how many references are possibly predatory
    * hastemporal bool - whether publication year statistics are known
    * temporal array - the temporal and citation statistics, as label and value pairs

    Example context (json):
    {
        "heading": "Reference check report",
        "assignmentlabel": "Assignment",
        "assignment": "Essay 2",
        "subjectlabel": "Student",
        "subject": "Ada Lovelace",
        "checkedlabel": "Checked",
        "checked": "1 July 2026, 9:14 AM",
        "downloadedlabel": "Downloaded",
        "downloaded": "2 July 2026, 4:30 PM",
        "iscomplete": true,
        "statuslabel": "Complete",
        "hassectionheading": true,
        "sectionheading": "References were read from the section headed \"References\".",
        "istruncated": false,
        "truncatednotice": "",
        "stats": [
            {"label": "References", "value": 16},
            {"label": "Verified", "value": 12}
        ],
        "hasretracted": false,
        "retractedlabel": "Retracted",
        "retracted": 0,
        "haspredatory": false,
        "predatorylabel": "Possibly predatory",
        "predatory": 0,
        "hastemporal": true,
        "temporal": [
            {"label": "Oldest", "value": "1998"},
            {"label": "Newest", "value": "2025"}
        ]
    }
}}
<h1 style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;">{{heading}}</h1>

<table cellpadding="2">
    <tr>
        <td style="width: 25%; font-weight: bold;">{{assignmentlabel}}</td>
        <td style="width: 75%;">{{assignment}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="width: 25%; font-weight: bold;">{{subjectlabel}}</td>
        <td style="width: 75%;">{{subject}}</td>
    </tr>
    {{#checked}}
        <tr>
            <td style="width: 25%; font-weight: bold;">{{checkedlabel}}</td>
            <td style="width: 75%;">{{checked}}</td>
        </tr>
    {{/checked}}
    <tr>
        <td style="width: 25%; font-weight: bold;">{{downloadedlabel}}</td>
        <td style="width: 75%;">{{downloaded}}</td>
    </tr>
</table>

{{^iscomplete}}
    <p style="color: #997404;">{{statuslabel}}</p>
{{/iscomplete}}

{{#hassectionheading}}
    <p style="font-size: 8pt; color: #5c636a;">{{sectionheading}}</p>
{{/hassectionheading}}

{{#istruncated}}
    <p style="font-size: 8pt; color: #997404;">{{truncatednotice}}</p>
{{/istruncated}}

<table cellpadding="4">
    <tr>
        {{#stats}}
            <td style="width: 16%; text-align: center; border: 0.5px solid #adb5bd; background-color: #f1f3f5; font-size: 8pt;">{{label}}</td>
        {{/stats}}
    </tr>
    <tr>
        {{#stats}}
            <td style="width: 16%; text-align: center; border: 0.5px solid #adb5bd; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold;">{{value}}</td>
        {{/stats}}
    </tr>
</table>

{{#hasretracted}}
    <p style="color: #b02a37; font-weight: bold;">{{retractedlabel}}: {{retracted}}</p>
{{/hasretracted}}

{{#haspredatory}}
    <p style="color: #997404; font-weight: bold;">{{predatorylabel}}: {{predatory}}</p>
{{/haspredatory}}

{{#hastemporal}}
    <table cellpadding="2">
        <tr>
            {{#temporal}}
                <td style="width: 20%; font-size: 8pt; color: #5c636a;">{{label}}</td>
            {{/temporal}}
        </tr>
        <tr>
            {{#temporal}}
                <td style="width: 20%; font-size: 9pt;">{{value}}</td>
            {{/temporal}}
        </tr>
    </table>
{{/hastemporal}}

<hr>
